{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "Thank you, Dr. Morgan. I'd like to share my findings from the technology review. My review confirms that personal phones cannot be used for school recordings. The project must use district tablets, store the source files in the restricted OralHistory drive, and delete recordings exactly 45 days after the final class presentation. Storing source files in that drive does not prohibit publishing consented recordings on the public school website. Additionally, the technology plan must include a secure-storage configuration record. This means the current draft plan's use of personal phones and indefinite retention would both need to be modified."}
```

